    "created_at": "2016-04-21T16:56:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-21T16:56:28Z",
    "body": "Yeah, this is getting messier and messier.\n\nI wonder if, instead, we should just say that ::marker potentially exists on all elements and gets generated when you set its `content` to something other than `none`.  This would make it act exactly like ::before, just still with a restricted set of properties that can apply to it.\n\nThen `display: list-item` changes from _creating_ the ::marker to just making the marker respond to the `list-style-*` properties.  On any other element, ::marker ignores those, and is just a restricted variant of ::before.\n\nI'll bring this up on the list.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
