    "body": "@aethanyc That seems like a pretty obscure case, and also if it was `list-style-position: outside` as you are suggesting we make it, then the layout would be pretty weird. See [example](http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?%3C!DOCTYPE%20html%3E%0A%3Cstyle%3E*%20%7B%20border%3A%201px%20silver%20solid%3B%20%7D%3C%2Fstyle%3E%0A%3Cdetails%3E%3Csummary%3E%3Ch1%20style%3D%22display%3A%20list-item%3B%20list-style%3A%20square%22%3EOutside%3C%2Fh1%3E%3C%2Fsummary%3E%3C%2Fdetails%3E%0Avs%0A%3Cdetails%3E%3Csummary%3E%3Ch1%20style%3D%22display%3A%20list-item%3B%20list-style%3A%20inside%20square%22%3EInside%3C%2Fh1%3E%3C%2Fsummary%3C%2Fdetails%3E%0A). I don't think we are doing anyone a disservice by making `list-style-position: inside` within a SUMMARY element, as it requires a significant amount of styling to result in something usable anyway; and in fact it's probably a more sensible default anyway.",
